.TH SW 1 "December 2024" "sworkflow 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sw \- streamlined Linux kernel compilation tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sw
.I command
.RI [ device ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sworkflow
(sw) is an automated kernel compilation tool designed to streamline the
process of compiling the Linux kernel and significantly reduce the overhead
involved in setting up the development environment.
.PP
It manages device-specific build configurations, cross-compiler setup,
and can package kernels using AnyKernel3.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR build ", " b " " \fIdevice\fR
Build the kernel for the specified device. Must be run from within a
kernel source tree. The device configuration is loaded from the config
file matching the device name.
.TP
.BR doctor ", " d " [" \fIdevice\fR "]"
Show available device configurations and their settings. When run without
a device argument, lists all available configs and their locations. When
a device is specified, displays the detailed configuration for that device
including architecture, defconfig, compiler settings, and build options.
Also indicates whether the current directory is a kernel source tree.
.TP
.BR init ", " i
Interactively generate a new device configuration file. Prompts for
device name, architecture, defconfig, cross-compiler paths, and other
build options.
.TP
.BR pack ", " p " " \fIdevice\fR
Package the compiled kernel (not yet implemented).
.TP
.BR help ", " h
Display help message with available commands.
.TP
.BR version ", " v
Display version information.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Device configurations are TOML files. They are parsed as data and never
executed, so a config file cannot run code.
.PP
They are searched in the following order:
.TP
1.
.I ./
(current directory)
.TP
2.
.I /etc/sworkflow/
(system installation) or
.I ~/.local/sw/configs/
(user installation)
.TP
3.
.I ./configs/
(configs subdirectory)
.PP
Configuration files are named
.BR sworkflow. \fIdevice\fR .toml
.PP
Within a directory a
.I .toml
config takes precedence over a legacy
.I .config
shell file of the same name. Shell configs are still read for
compatibility but are deprecated, and
.B sw init
only writes TOML.
.SS Inheritance
A config may name one parent with the top level
.B extends
key, resolved against the same search path with
.I .toml
appended. Profiles ship under
.I base/
and
.I soc/
of a config directory, so an
.B extends
of soc/lito reads
.IR soc/lito.toml .
.PP
A parent may itself extend another. Tables merge key by key, so a child
replaces only what it names, and lists concatenate with the parent's
entries first. Cycles are an error.
.SS Expansion
String values may contain
.BR ${kernel.root} ,
the kernel tree being built, and
.BR ${env.NAME} ,
a named environment variable. Expansion substitutes known names only and
never invokes a shell.
.SS Schema
.TP
.B schema
Schema version. Required, currently 1. A config declaring a version sw
does not know is refused rather than partly understood.
.TP
.B extends
Profile to inherit from. Optional.
.TP
.B [device]
.IR name ,
.IR vendor ,
.IR aliases ,
.IR board_platform .
The last is exported as TARGET_BOARD_PLATFORM.
.TP
.B [kernel]
.IR arch ,
.IR defconfig_arch ,
.IR defconfigs ,
.IR image .
.I arch
and
.I defconfigs
are required.
.I defconfig_arch
names the architecture whose configs directory holds the defconfigs when
it differs from
.IR arch ,
such as x86 for an x86_64 build.
.I image
is the built image under arch/<arch>/boot.
.TP
.B [toolchain]
.IR cross_compile ,
.IR cross_compile_arm32 ,
.IR clang ,
.IR env .
.I clang
is a boolean.
.I env
is a table of variables placed in the build environment.
.TP
.B [build]
.IR modules ,
.IR dist ,
.IR clean ,
.IR silent ,
.IR out_dir .
All booleans except
.IR out_dir ,
which defaults to out.
.TP
.B [dtbo]
.IR enabled ,
.IR page_size ,
.IR path .
.I path
is a glob relative to the build output directory.
.TP
.B [anykernel]
.I enabled
and
.IR branch ,
for AnyKernel3 packaging.
.TP
.B [external_modules]
.I root
and
.IR paths .
Out-of-tree module directories, built in the order given, resolved
against
.IR root .
Suffix an entry with :kbuild when it builds from the kernel tree rather
than its own.
.TP
.B [meta]
.I maintainer
and
.IR tested_tree .
Provenance only, unused by the build.
.PP
An unknown section, an unknown key, or a value of the wrong type is an
error rather than something quietly ignored.
.SS Example
.PP
.RS
.nf
schema = 1
extends = "soc/lito"

[device]
name = "gauguin"
vendor = "xiaomi"

[kernel]
defconfigs = ["vendor/lito-perf_defconfig", "vendor/xiaomi/gauguin.config"]
.fi
.RE
.PP
See
.I sworkflow_template.toml
in a config directory for every key with its default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/sw
Main executable (system installation).
.TP
.I /usr/share/sworkflow/src/
Source modules (system installation).
.TP
.I /usr/share/sworkflow/utils/
Utility scripts including mkdtboimg.py and swconfig.py, the config
loader.
.TP
.I /etc/sworkflow/
System-wide device configurations.
.TP
.I /etc/sworkflow/base/, /etc/sworkflow/soc/
Profiles that device configs inherit through
.BR extends .
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/sw
Main executable (user installation).
.TP
.I ~/.local/sw/
User installation directory.
.TP
.I sworkflow.<device>.toml
Device-specific configuration file.
.TP
.I sworkflow_template.toml
Reference listing every key with its default.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SW_SRC_DIR
Directory holding
.I src/
and
.IR utils/ .
.TP
.B SW_CONFIG_DIR
Directory searched for device configs and profiles.
.PP
Both are worked out by
.B sw
from the installation it detects and exported for the modules it runs.
They are not read from the calling environment, so setting them
beforehand has no effect.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 22
Invalid argument or missing required configuration.
.TP
.B 125
Operation cancelled or configuration error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build kernel for mainline x86_64:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd /path/to/linux
sw build mainline
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build kernel for ARM64 device:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd /path/to/kernel-source
sw b X00P-3.18
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a new device configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sw init
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check version:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sw version
.fi
.RE
.PP
List available configs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sw doctor
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show detailed config for a device:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sw d billie
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1),
.BR gcc (1),
.BR clang (1)
